      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A consultant's personality and communication style play a pivotal role in garnering respect within elite business circles. Certain personality traits, such as confidence, charisma, and being seen as a reliable thought leader, tend to command more respect. On the other hand, excessive predisposition towards rationality over relational elements can sometimes arise as a hindrance. In interacting with board members, a consultant who combines authoritative knowledge with emotional intelligence could establish a firmer footing. Moreover, a consultant with an air of unshakeable confidence, when coupled with a genuine interest in others, can create an invaluable connection space. This blend of seemingly steadfast optimism with a commitment to understanding and addressing the concerns of others can influence one's perceived trustworthiness and authority within those critical boardroom discussions. It's this nuanced combination of professional reliability with empathetic engagement that can often engender immediate trust, even amidst inevitable scrutiny in professional circles.",
